From 6afc7de399b74e5576bd2be61713e79c880e0e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:47:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Allow Korean homonyms; tolerate part-of-speech labels in
 imports

- migrations/0002: unique on the (ko_norm, bg_norm) pair instead of ko_norm alone
- server: ON CONFLICT on the pair; duplicate message names the pair
- practice: typing another meaning of the same prompt asks you to try again
  instead of counting as wrong; feedback lists the other meanings
- import: part of speech accepted in English, Bulgarian or Korean; unknown
  labels are left empty and reported instead of failing the batch
- tests for sharesAlternative and parsePos; README notes
---
